      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-pulcher-2/",
      "html": "<p>The pikehead, Luciocephalus pulcher, is a highly specialized anabantoid, a relative of the chocolate gouramies. Like the latter the pikehead is a mouthbrooder. Luciocephalus is the only true predator among the various anabantoids; in its natural habitat it feeds preferably on shrimps.</p><p>The calm, beautiful animal (Latin pulcher = beautiful) would surely be a favourite aquarium fish despite being always hungry, but there is a big problem: Luciocephalus is among the most sensitive fish of all.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-pulcher-2/",
      "html": "<p>The most current importation of the fish is absolutely problem-free. The adult pikeheads, about 11-13 cm long, were obtained via Singapore. The collecting site is unknown, as the pikeheads are not only extraordinarily healthy but also extraordinarily coloured.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-pulcher-2/",
      "html": "<p>Usually the pikehead has a broad, horizontal brown band along the flanks. Only when the fish are under distress or during mating this band vanishes and irregular spots are visible. The new importation has shown this spotted pattern since arrival 10 days ago. There is no satisfying explanation for the phenomenon; maybe it is currently the breeding season for pikeheads?</p>"
    }
  ],
